WEBVTT

00:15.724 --> 00:17.934
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

00:19.394 --> 00:21.438
EPISODE 6

00:21.521 --> 00:23.940
What? The July on-call schedule's
out already?

00:24.024 --> 00:25.734
Yeah, you should check it now too.

00:25.817 --> 00:26.985
You're so quick.

00:28.695 --> 00:30.113
KU DO-WON

00:30.196 --> 00:33.158
KU DO-WON, OH YI-YOUNG

00:39.622 --> 00:41.499
I guess Sa-bi doesn't know everything.

00:44.419 --> 00:46.254
It's called the law
of total patient volume.

00:46.337 --> 00:47.881
The total number of patients we'll see

00:47.964 --> 00:49.507
-is already set.
-What do you mean?

00:49.591 --> 00:52.218
A resident sees too many patients
and fills their quota.

00:52.302 --> 00:54.304
Later, they open a practice.
But what will happen?

00:54.387 --> 00:56.431
It would fail,
because they have no patients.

00:56.514 --> 00:57.432
That's right.

00:57.515 --> 00:59.976
-What's that have to do with on-call duty?
-Right.

01:00.060 --> 01:03.313
Every time I'm with Dr. Myeong,
patients come in like crazy.

01:03.897 --> 01:05.940
I'm using up so much of my total quota.

01:06.024 --> 01:07.525
I need a lot for my practice later.

01:08.443 --> 01:09.652
But I'm on call twice in July.

01:09.736 --> 01:10.779
That's nonsense.

01:11.279 --> 01:13.156
You just don't want
to work with Dr. Myeong.

01:13.239 --> 01:14.240
Well, you're not wrong.

01:14.741 --> 01:17.368
Hey, I may open a practice in the future,

01:17.452 --> 01:19.662
so can't you switch
with me just once? Please?

01:20.497 --> 01:21.623
I checked,

01:21.706 --> 01:23.958
and you had zero shifts
with Dr. Myeong in June.

01:24.042 --> 01:25.168
That's why it's twice.

01:26.294 --> 01:27.837
I can't believe you checked that.

01:30.215 --> 01:31.049
Hey, Sa-bi.

01:33.092 --> 01:35.261
This is your day, and this is my day.

01:35.345 --> 01:36.930
Couldn't you switch with me just once?

01:39.599 --> 01:40.892
You think I don't know?

01:43.228 --> 01:44.395
You want Dr. Ku…

01:48.107 --> 01:49.567
since he's easy to work with, right?

01:50.610 --> 01:52.362
He takes most of the calls

01:52.445 --> 01:53.822
and even lets you nap.

01:54.697 --> 01:56.574
That's not the only reason.

01:56.658 --> 01:57.784
Then what is it?

01:57.867 --> 01:59.077
What?

02:02.330 --> 02:04.833
It's a Friday. I need to go home
and watch my show.

02:04.916 --> 02:07.210
Watch the rerun.
That's not a good reason to switch.

02:09.170 --> 02:11.673
Hey, what is this?
Sa-bi, you didn't schedule this right.

02:11.756 --> 02:13.216
I'm the only one on call nine times.

02:13.299 --> 02:14.717
Yi-young and Sa-bi have eight,

02:14.801 --> 02:16.052
and Jae-il has seven.

02:16.136 --> 02:17.011
Oh, that?

02:17.095 --> 02:18.680
You were sick on June 8.

02:18.763 --> 02:20.765
Jae-il covered for you then.

02:20.849 --> 02:23.143
-Right.
-You have to repay him for that.

02:24.269 --> 02:25.103
Hey, Jae-il.

02:26.688 --> 02:28.606
Can I repay you in August instead?

02:29.107 --> 02:30.150
No!

02:33.444 --> 02:34.529
Hey.

02:35.238 --> 02:36.781
I was really sick that day.

02:37.365 --> 02:39.742
I was here but had no time to be treated.

02:39.826 --> 02:42.495
I had a high fever and was so weak.

02:42.579 --> 02:45.957
I was in my parka
and passed out in the on-call room.

02:47.041 --> 02:47.959
Then, in August--

02:48.042 --> 02:49.752
No! Repay him in July!

02:49.836 --> 02:51.838
"Shirked on-call shifts
are repaid the next month."

02:51.921 --> 02:52.881
That's our rule.

02:52.964 --> 02:54.132
We have a rule like that?

02:54.716 --> 02:55.633
Rule, my foot.

02:55.717 --> 02:58.011
Jae-il, please?

02:58.094 --> 03:00.388
Just this once.
I promise to repay you in August.

03:00.972 --> 03:02.181
-Okay.
-No.

03:02.265 --> 03:03.558
You'll end up not repaying him.

03:03.641 --> 03:04.475
What?

03:04.559 --> 03:06.352
It happened to me a lot as an intern.

03:06.436 --> 03:07.520
I'm not like that.

03:07.604 --> 03:09.314
Exactly, so repay him right away.

03:09.898 --> 03:12.317
If you switch shifts,
it messes up the schedule's fairness.

03:12.400 --> 03:15.194
Hey, why are you being
so strict with on-call shifts?

03:15.278 --> 03:17.572
I made this with even weekends
and off days in mind.

03:18.156 --> 03:19.240
There you go again.

03:19.782 --> 03:22.201
Why are you being so uptight
over something so minor?

03:22.285 --> 03:23.786
And there you go again.

03:23.870 --> 03:26.331
I'm going by the rules.
Why are you getting angry again?

03:26.414 --> 03:27.874
-I got angry?
-Yeah.

03:27.957 --> 03:29.292
You're just being uptight!

03:29.375 --> 03:31.419
I was being uptight because you got angry.

03:31.502 --> 03:33.421
I got angry
because you were being uptight.

03:33.504 --> 03:34.881
All I did was make the schedule.

03:34.964 --> 03:37.634
-You're so frustrating. Seriously.
-You make me frustrated too.

03:37.717 --> 03:39.510
-The same goes for me.
-Then let's not talk.

03:39.594 --> 03:41.012
-Fine.
-I'm not changing it.

03:42.180 --> 03:45.141
They're always fighting these days.
Is it the heat?

03:45.225 --> 03:47.393
Heat? The AC's on full blast.

03:48.061 --> 03:50.688
Did being overworked and sleep-deprived
make them both cranky?

03:50.772 --> 03:51.606
No.

03:52.190 --> 03:53.233
They just don't get along.

03:54.817 --> 03:55.944
They'll figure it out.

03:56.569 --> 03:57.403
This affects us.

03:57.487 --> 03:58.613
It's not my business.

03:59.656 --> 04:01.991
Leave them be.
It's not our place to intervene.

04:05.328 --> 04:06.162
Yes, Doctor?

04:06.955 --> 04:09.123
Yes, I'll be there. I have time.

04:09.749 --> 04:10.750
Okay, bye.

04:11.376 --> 04:12.460
Hey, you go on ahead.

04:14.045 --> 04:15.588
-Actually, a few weeks ago--
-Bye.

04:16.381 --> 04:17.215
Bye.

05:00.216 --> 05:01.217
Geez!

05:03.761 --> 05:04.637
Hey, Joo-young.

05:04.721 --> 05:05.722
Are you going to be late?

05:05.805 --> 05:07.181
Our reservation time's almost up.

05:07.265 --> 05:08.391
I'll be there soon.

05:08.474 --> 05:10.101
Do-won's not there yet, right?

05:10.184 --> 05:11.102
He's here.

05:11.978 --> 05:13.855
He is? His car's here though.

05:13.938 --> 05:14.897
He took the subway.

05:14.981 --> 05:16.482
He said traffic gets bad on Fridays.

05:16.566 --> 05:18.109
Why are you telling me this now?

05:35.543 --> 05:38.755
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

05:44.802 --> 05:46.554
Prof. Jo's not here yet, right?

05:46.637 --> 05:47.472
No.

05:50.558 --> 05:51.976
You were on-call yesterday, right?

05:52.060 --> 05:52.894
Yeah.

05:52.977 --> 05:55.772
Did you talk to Ms. Park Jeong-ju
during post-op rounds?

05:56.606 --> 05:57.607
What did she say?

06:01.611 --> 06:05.031
She had a hysterectomy for fibroids,
but had her ovaries removed too.

06:05.114 --> 06:08.201
"Park Jeong-ju, age 54,
TLH and BSO performed due to myoma."

06:08.284 --> 06:09.118
Her?

06:09.202 --> 06:11.662
Yeah. The professor said to visit her

06:11.746 --> 06:13.998
and explain to her
what the procedure was again.

06:14.082 --> 06:16.167
The professor said that to you.

06:17.335 --> 06:19.337
No, he said it to you.

06:19.420 --> 06:20.838
No, it was you.

06:21.506 --> 06:24.217
It says right here.
"Ward out at 6:30 p.m."

06:25.218 --> 06:26.052
What?

06:26.135 --> 06:28.096
She arrived here at 6:30 p.m.,

06:28.179 --> 06:30.098
so it's during the day,
which is your shift.

06:30.181 --> 06:31.516
That doesn't make sense.

06:31.599 --> 06:33.893
Why is 6:30 p.m. the day shift?
It's the on-call shift.

06:33.976 --> 06:36.938
To be exact,
the on-call shift starts at 6:31 p.m.

06:37.021 --> 06:40.316
If you want to be cheap like that,
then the day shift ends at 6:29:59 p.m.

06:40.399 --> 06:43.361
The patient in Room 1014
was vomiting blood then, so I was there.

06:43.444 --> 06:45.530
I was busy too
and had a patient in the ICU, okay?

06:45.613 --> 06:46.823
I thought you did it.

06:46.906 --> 06:48.074
I thought you would do it.

06:49.617 --> 06:52.328
Oh, no. The professor's going to be
doing rounds soon.

06:53.246 --> 06:54.413
Hey, first-years.

06:55.123 --> 06:56.207
Didn't I tell you yesterday

06:56.290 --> 06:58.209
to explain to Ms. Park
how the surgery went?

06:59.168 --> 07:00.628
Why is she asking me today

07:00.711 --> 07:02.338
if her ovaries are still there?

07:06.884 --> 07:07.844
Hey!

07:08.886 --> 07:10.263
Who's the attending doctor?

07:13.057 --> 07:14.392
I am.

07:15.893 --> 07:16.727
I'm sorry, sir.

07:19.147 --> 07:20.440
I was going to do it--

07:20.523 --> 07:21.357
Too busy, right?

07:21.441 --> 07:22.775
That's why you didn't do it?

07:23.359 --> 07:24.485
But you're not the only one.

07:24.569 --> 07:26.028
Everyone here is just as busy.

07:26.112 --> 07:27.488
You call that your excuse?!

07:28.948 --> 07:30.032
I'm sorry.

07:40.209 --> 07:42.712
Gosh, we didn't know you were here.
I'm sorry.

07:43.546 --> 07:45.173
Why the wheelchair all of a sudden?

07:45.256 --> 07:46.174
Did you fall?

07:46.757 --> 07:49.427
Her feet were swollen this morning,
so her shoes didn't fit.

07:49.510 --> 07:51.345
I thought walking barefoot would hurt.

07:51.429 --> 07:52.680
Just a second.

07:53.848 --> 07:54.807
Be careful.

07:54.891 --> 07:57.018
-Give it a rest.
-Okay. Be careful.

07:57.101 --> 07:59.854
I'm sorry. We'll put it back right away.

08:03.399 --> 08:05.109
The professor asked me
to explain once more

08:05.193 --> 08:06.819
what she said during outpatient care.

08:07.403 --> 08:09.489
She said you were shocked,
so you may not remember.

08:09.572 --> 08:11.949
Gosh, that scary news again?

08:12.533 --> 08:15.161
You've undergone
dilation and curettage several times,

08:15.244 --> 08:17.121
and since you have placenta previa,

08:17.205 --> 08:19.165
heavy bleeding is expected during surgery.

08:19.999 --> 08:22.001
If bleeding persists
after the placenta's removed,

08:22.084 --> 08:24.420
a balloon will be inserted
into the uterus to stop it.

08:27.340 --> 08:29.842
You know how we use tissues
to stop nosebleeds?

08:30.426 --> 08:32.678
The balloon will be used in a similar way

08:32.762 --> 08:33.804
to stop the bleeding.

08:34.305 --> 08:35.932
But if bleeding still persists,

08:36.015 --> 08:38.142
we'll insert a catheter into your thigh

08:38.226 --> 08:41.395
and perform a uterine artery embolization
to block blood flow.

08:42.063 --> 08:45.233
And if that doesn't work,
the uterus must be removed.

08:46.526 --> 08:48.110
Don't worry, that won't happen.

08:48.194 --> 08:50.446
If we do either
of the last two procedures I mentioned,

08:50.530 --> 08:52.448
we'll inform your husband during surgery

08:52.532 --> 08:54.242
to obtain additional consent then.

08:54.325 --> 08:55.159
All right.

08:57.537 --> 08:58.871
Doctor…

08:58.955 --> 09:01.749
Please take good care of my baby.

09:02.458 --> 09:04.001
The baby is very healthy.

09:04.085 --> 09:06.295
We're monitoring it daily.

09:06.379 --> 09:08.965
No, I mean my wife.

09:09.465 --> 09:10.341
What?

09:10.424 --> 09:11.467
Don't.

09:15.846 --> 09:17.807
Yes, of course.

09:24.063 --> 09:25.439
Goodness.

09:25.523 --> 09:27.233
Don't worry. Everything will go well.

09:36.409 --> 09:37.660
So sweet, right?

09:39.495 --> 09:41.247
Yes, very.

09:42.164 --> 09:45.084
So sweet and warm.

09:45.751 --> 09:47.253
How can you get that warm?

09:47.837 --> 09:49.005
You add hot water.

09:51.299 --> 09:53.301
The smell of love is in the air.

09:53.384 --> 09:54.802
It smells like apples to me.

09:56.637 --> 09:58.222
I mean Ms. Cha Bo-mi's husband.

09:59.432 --> 10:01.267
I was talking about him.

10:03.102 --> 10:05.187
He gave us this tea too.

10:05.271 --> 10:06.897
It was for taking care of his baby.

10:08.983 --> 10:11.193
I've worked
in the OB ward for seven years,

10:11.277 --> 10:14.155
but I've never seen
a kinder, sweeter husband.

10:16.490 --> 10:17.783
Where do you find men like that?

10:17.867 --> 10:19.035
There are a few.

10:19.577 --> 10:21.162
I don't know if that's good though.

10:21.245 --> 10:23.748
Where? Where on earth are they?

10:25.041 --> 10:25.916
At my house.

10:32.340 --> 10:34.592
Do-won's heading into surgery.
He says he's sorry.

10:35.259 --> 10:36.552
Sorry for what?

10:36.636 --> 10:38.638
Egg retrieval is nothing special.

10:38.721 --> 10:40.473
It's my fifth time. I'm not even nervous.

10:40.556 --> 10:42.308
Should I call your sister?

10:42.391 --> 10:43.225
Don't.

10:43.309 --> 10:45.603
I don't want anything to disrupt my peace.

10:45.686 --> 10:47.021
I didn't tell her on purpose.

10:52.985 --> 10:54.987
She looks about seven months in.

10:56.405 --> 10:58.949
Seven months? Gosh, it's rough.

10:59.033 --> 11:02.370
At that stage,
they say your back, ribs, feet…

11:02.453 --> 11:03.329
Everything hurts.

11:03.412 --> 11:05.289
I heard it's really hard.

11:05.373 --> 11:06.499
How would you know?

11:06.582 --> 11:07.958
I looked it up.

11:13.673 --> 11:15.758
It looks like they're here to give birth.

11:15.841 --> 11:17.343
Birth? Gosh.

11:18.552 --> 11:20.262
After the birth, everyone says

11:20.346 --> 11:21.764
that pregnancy is a piece of cake.

11:21.847 --> 11:23.599
The real hell is taking care of the baby.

11:24.350 --> 11:26.018
They say parents age a year each day.

11:26.727 --> 11:28.062
I don't want to get old.

11:28.145 --> 11:29.563
Right? Me neither.

11:30.147 --> 11:32.942
Should we just cancel and go home?

11:33.025 --> 11:33.859
No.

11:34.902 --> 11:35.903
I'm still going to do it.

11:36.570 --> 11:37.655
I'm doing it.

11:40.574 --> 11:42.535
I told you not to feel bad.

11:43.119 --> 11:45.121
I'm not doing it for you.

11:45.204 --> 11:47.748
And it's not because
of your mother's nagging either.

11:47.832 --> 11:49.583
I'm doing it for me.

11:49.667 --> 11:51.419
It's because I want to do it.

11:51.502 --> 11:53.212
I want to become a mother.

11:54.171 --> 11:56.549
I'm just afraid
it'll be hard on you like last time.

11:57.842 --> 11:59.009
It won't be.

11:59.093 --> 12:00.845
The saying goes
"all's well that ends well."

12:00.928 --> 12:02.346
It'll be a beautiful finish.

12:05.391 --> 12:06.976
This will be the last time for sure.

12:08.227 --> 12:09.562
Whether it's three or four eggs,

12:10.563 --> 12:13.232
I'll do only
as much as needed for fertilization.

12:14.024 --> 12:16.402
After that, I'm not doing it. I won't.

12:21.866 --> 12:23.325
Keep your chin up too.

12:23.409 --> 12:24.743
I'm not doing anything.

12:24.827 --> 12:25.870
I'm fine.

12:25.953 --> 12:27.496
I'm fine too.

12:27.580 --> 12:30.166
The shot in my stomach
didn't hurt much today.

12:31.208 --> 12:34.795
I'll be asleep for the procedure,
so when I wake up, it'll be over.

12:37.840 --> 12:39.216
It's time. Should we go in?

12:40.134 --> 12:41.343
Yeah.

12:46.265 --> 12:48.100
Ms. Oh, you may go in.

12:56.650 --> 12:59.028
It's 3:40 p.m. now.
We only have 20 minutes left.

12:59.111 --> 13:00.613
I'm going down again.

13:00.696 --> 13:02.114
You're going up, right?

13:02.198 --> 13:03.532
Yes, I am.

13:04.074 --> 13:05.618
But I think I'm going to die.

13:05.701 --> 13:08.704
You only did four prescriptions,
while I did nine?

13:08.787 --> 13:10.247
Hurry up, will you?

13:10.331 --> 13:11.957
We still have six patients left!

13:12.041 --> 13:14.084
This is the fastest I can go.

13:14.168 --> 13:15.085
I'm sorry.

13:15.169 --> 13:17.338
If we don't end before 4:00 p.m.
and chemo is delayed,

13:17.421 --> 13:18.923
you know it'll be chaos, don't you?

13:19.006 --> 13:20.174
Yes, I know.

13:20.257 --> 13:22.551
And we'll be the first to die
if that happens.

13:22.635 --> 13:24.970
Dr. Jo will mow us down with his mouth.

13:26.680 --> 13:28.557
Wait, BSA is 1.5.

13:28.641 --> 13:30.226
So 1.5 times 135 is…

13:30.309 --> 13:31.227
It's 202.5.

13:31.310 --> 13:32.478
What? Are you a genius?

13:32.561 --> 13:34.355
As Um Jay,
my special talent was mental math,

13:34.438 --> 13:35.940
so I'd compete against calculators.

13:36.023 --> 13:37.733
Hey, keep your hands on the keyboard.

13:37.816 --> 13:39.360
Our hands aren't important right now.

13:39.443 --> 13:41.028
Our necks are on the line.

13:41.111 --> 13:42.238
I'm sorry.

13:42.321 --> 13:43.656
Hello, all.

13:43.739 --> 13:44.990
Hello, Professor!

13:45.658 --> 13:48.577
I have a meeting this afternoon,
so I was thinking of doing rounds

13:48.661 --> 13:50.746
for patients who had surgery this morning.

13:50.829 --> 13:52.498
-I see! Right.
-Right.

13:52.581 --> 13:53.499
But we can't.

13:54.458 --> 13:55.543
Who would dare

13:55.626 --> 13:58.295
to thoughtlessly do rounds
at 3:40 p.m. in the GYN ward?

13:59.380 --> 14:00.631
They've lost their minds.

14:01.966 --> 14:04.260
I've lost my mind. I apologize.

14:04.343 --> 14:06.095
Good luck. Continue what you were doing.

14:06.178 --> 14:07.513
-Thank you!
-Thank you!

14:08.097 --> 14:09.515
Hurry! Come on!

14:10.516 --> 14:11.684
Damn it.

14:11.767 --> 14:13.102
Good, we're still okay.

14:13.185 --> 14:14.937
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

14:22.570 --> 14:23.404
Geez.

14:24.405 --> 14:25.656
YEOM
ATTENDING DOCTOR: KIM SA-BI

14:25.739 --> 14:27.116
Hello.

14:27.199 --> 14:28.367
Hello.

14:32.079 --> 14:33.706
You seem to always listen to this song.

14:34.331 --> 14:36.166
It's my favorite hymn.

14:37.084 --> 14:39.211
I see. You're Catholic.

14:39.295 --> 14:41.422
What about you, Doctor?
Do you have a religion?

14:41.505 --> 14:43.674
Yes, mine's shamanism.

14:44.717 --> 14:47.052
Last month,
I followed the Great Orb Fairy.

14:47.136 --> 14:49.388
But this month,
I switched to Gangnam Young Master.

14:49.471 --> 14:50.598
They're truly mystical.

14:52.141 --> 14:53.601
How are you feeling?

14:53.684 --> 14:55.853
Are you having any trouble breathing?

14:56.604 --> 14:57.438
I'm fine.

14:58.022 --> 15:00.149
You must be busy. Why come by so often?

15:00.232 --> 15:02.818
Come on, I have to see you if you're here.

15:02.902 --> 15:04.320
You were my first patient.

15:05.446 --> 15:07.656
And thanks to you, I didn't run away.

15:08.365 --> 15:09.199
Right.

15:10.075 --> 15:11.660
You ran away, but you came back.

15:11.744 --> 15:12.912
You thought I was dead.

15:12.995 --> 15:14.038
Dead?

15:14.121 --> 15:15.205
That's not it.

15:15.831 --> 15:17.374
I knew nothing then.

15:17.458 --> 15:19.251
I came back because I was so scared.

15:19.335 --> 15:21.337
I was a total fool back in March.

15:22.421 --> 15:24.924
Still, it seems you have
a better handle on things now.

15:25.007 --> 15:26.050
You look much better.

15:26.133 --> 15:27.551
It's not the case at all.

15:28.427 --> 15:31.096
When I got used to the work,
things got busier.

15:33.265 --> 15:34.266
Work is one thing,

15:35.059 --> 15:36.977
but people stress me out these days.

15:37.061 --> 15:38.520
Who? Patients?

15:39.688 --> 15:40.606
The professors?

15:41.523 --> 15:43.442
No, my colleagues.

15:45.527 --> 15:47.363
I have the worst luck with colleagues.

15:48.405 --> 15:51.492
One has an attitude,
and another's all over the place.

15:51.575 --> 15:52.993
The last one lacks a human touch.

15:53.077 --> 15:55.412
They're also inflexible
and have zero empathy.

15:56.372 --> 15:58.791
It's like talking to a robot, not a human.

15:59.667 --> 16:02.711
And they have an opinion
on even the smallest things.

16:02.795 --> 16:03.796
They're always saying,

16:04.296 --> 16:06.256
"I read this in a textbook, so I know."

16:06.840 --> 16:08.884
They think they're always right.

16:09.927 --> 16:12.846
It's just so frustrating.
I can't talk to them.

16:13.430 --> 16:15.349
We're completely incompatible.

16:17.142 --> 16:19.061
The professor already came by
on their rounds.

16:21.480 --> 16:22.731
These aren't rounds.

16:22.815 --> 16:25.734
I was asked to explain
the CT scan results again.

16:25.818 --> 16:27.444
The imaging came up normal

16:27.528 --> 16:29.405
and tumor marker levels
are also decreasing,

16:29.488 --> 16:31.615
so this round of chemo should go well too.

16:32.449 --> 16:33.283
I see.

16:34.326 --> 16:35.452
I'll let you rest now.

16:46.505 --> 16:47.506
I'm screwed.

16:50.092 --> 16:50.968
Here.

17:03.313 --> 17:04.773
I don't really like pigs' trotters.

17:04.857 --> 17:06.525
I got it because Sa-bi wanted it.

17:06.608 --> 17:07.776
Just eat.

17:09.111 --> 17:11.155
Hey, I thought you had dinner plans today.

17:11.238 --> 17:13.365
I have some time. I'll just have a taste.

17:14.825 --> 17:17.453
But you did wash your hands, right?

17:17.536 --> 17:18.537
Yes.

17:18.620 --> 17:21.206
I washed them
as thoroughly as I do when I scrub in.

17:21.290 --> 17:22.249
Just my hair's dirty.

17:23.709 --> 17:26.045
You didn't go home again?
You weren't on call.

17:27.463 --> 17:29.131
You might not believe it,

17:30.049 --> 17:33.218
but every night these days,
a sort of voluntary on-call shift--

17:33.302 --> 17:35.429
Right! Who's making the August schedule?

17:37.389 --> 17:39.933
Hey, can you take me off
for the third weekend?

17:40.017 --> 17:41.518
I'm telling you in advance, okay?

17:41.602 --> 17:43.645
My dad's birthday is on the third week,

17:43.729 --> 17:45.314
so I was going to ask you too.

17:46.190 --> 17:47.066
I'll think about it.

17:47.149 --> 17:49.985
You don't usually think much.
So why think now?

17:50.069 --> 17:51.236
Don't.

17:52.154 --> 17:54.323
Sa-bi, it's your dad's birthday?

17:55.282 --> 17:56.867
Hey, I asked first.

17:56.950 --> 17:58.702
What does that matter? It's up to her.

17:59.870 --> 18:02.414
Hey! Do you two have to fight
over the schedule every month?

18:03.499 --> 18:05.584
Yi-young, just be fair about it.

18:05.667 --> 18:07.711
You know the senior
on call the third week?

18:07.795 --> 18:09.880
Pick whoever gets along better with them.

18:10.589 --> 18:11.632
Gets along better?

18:11.715 --> 18:13.425
You know Dr. Woo from Orthopedics?

18:13.509 --> 18:16.428
He organizes the on-call schedule
based on compatibility.

18:17.012 --> 18:19.389
But amazingly,
whenever he organizes the schedule,

18:19.473 --> 18:21.141
the number of ER patients drop.

18:22.017 --> 18:22.851
-That's great!
-No!

18:22.935 --> 18:24.228
I'm Christian.

18:25.562 --> 18:27.022
It has nothing to do with religion.

18:27.106 --> 18:28.941
It also has nothing to do
with compatibility.

18:29.024 --> 18:30.442
We're just doing it for fun.

18:30.526 --> 18:32.569
We can't make the schedule based on fun.

18:33.779 --> 18:35.239
Right, since it's not fun,

18:35.322 --> 18:37.491
we should at least try
to make it fun this way.

18:37.574 --> 18:39.118
That won't make on-call duty more fun.

18:39.201 --> 18:40.828
So why would we need to do that?

18:42.830 --> 18:43.997
You're so frustrating.

18:44.081 --> 18:45.749
I feel the same. You frustrate me too.

18:53.048 --> 18:53.924
Yes, ma'am?

18:55.342 --> 18:57.678
Don't be sorry. I'm the grateful one.

18:58.846 --> 18:59.721
I'm leaving.

19:00.305 --> 19:02.474
I actually wanted to
get out of this place.

19:02.558 --> 19:03.600
Yes.

19:03.684 --> 19:04.810
Where are you going?

19:06.186 --> 19:07.312
KU DO-WON

19:08.522 --> 19:10.274
You two make an agreement.
I'm heading out.

19:10.816 --> 19:12.568
-Where are you going?
-Where are you going?

19:27.541 --> 19:29.084
ULTRASOUND ROOM

19:29.168 --> 19:30.335
Hello.

19:30.419 --> 19:31.670
Hello, Doctor.

19:33.130 --> 19:35.007
Thank you for remembering to call me.

19:36.008 --> 19:37.843
But were you unable to go home
because of me?

19:37.926 --> 19:39.261
Of course not.

19:39.970 --> 19:43.182
I'm busy organizing the imaging data,
so I'm stuck here all week.

19:44.308 --> 19:45.642
That must be really rough.

19:45.726 --> 19:48.061
I'm not the one
you should be worried about.

19:49.271 --> 19:50.397
Are you okay?

19:50.480 --> 19:51.899
You look really tired.

19:52.524 --> 19:54.568
I'm fine.
I'll look at the images and go sleep.

19:55.277 --> 19:57.988
By the way, if we do emergency imaging
on OB patients at night,

19:58.071 --> 19:59.364
you want me to keep calling you?

19:59.448 --> 20:00.699
Are you going to keep looking?

20:00.782 --> 20:02.993
Yes, I want to do it for a few more weeks.

20:03.869 --> 20:04.953
Could you help me out?

20:06.038 --> 20:08.290
Sure. It's not a big deal for me.

20:08.373 --> 20:09.791
Thank you.

20:09.875 --> 20:11.126
Around this time,

20:11.210 --> 20:13.921
all the first-years
always get very nervous.

20:14.004 --> 20:15.297
They want to do well.

20:16.465 --> 20:17.341
Not me.

20:18.508 --> 20:20.177
I'm not expecting to do well.

20:20.719 --> 20:22.721
I just want to pull my own weight.

20:24.097 --> 20:25.349
Doing that

20:25.891 --> 20:27.643
is my goal for this year.

20:33.315 --> 20:34.149
Yes?

20:34.733 --> 20:37.319
Dr. Eun-mi will be here soon.
Send the patient over.

20:38.403 --> 20:39.446
All right, bye.

20:41.615 --> 20:43.700
By the way, what brings the patient here?

20:44.743 --> 20:47.162
I'm sure it won't be anything serious.

20:47.246 --> 20:48.247
What?

20:48.330 --> 20:50.082
Do you know Ms. Moon Yeong-shin?

20:50.165 --> 20:51.959
She's very famous.

20:52.042 --> 20:54.169
I think she set the all-time OB record

20:54.253 --> 20:56.922
for the most number of ultrasounds.

20:57.005 --> 20:59.132
She comes at least once a week.

20:59.216 --> 21:01.927
And since a few months ago,
she comes twice a week at times.

21:02.511 --> 21:04.680
I just wonder
if you're being too sensitive.

21:05.264 --> 21:07.808
The doctors here seem annoyed with us now.

21:07.891 --> 21:09.226
Look, I know too.

21:09.810 --> 21:11.311
You think I don't?

21:12.062 --> 21:13.522
I don't want to be like this either.

21:13.605 --> 21:16.275
But I'm worried something
may be wrong with the baby.

21:18.777 --> 21:21.196
She doesn't seem to be
moving around as well as yesterday.

21:21.863 --> 21:24.908
My stomach hurts more than last time,
and it feels tight.

21:34.626 --> 21:36.169
She's really fine.

21:36.253 --> 21:38.005
The placenta's in a good spot too.

21:38.588 --> 21:40.090
The placenta's in good position too.

21:40.757 --> 21:42.092
She's not moving around much?

21:42.175 --> 21:43.010
No.

21:43.802 --> 21:45.762
Not as much as yesterday.

21:46.513 --> 21:48.223
And I have pain in the lower area.

21:51.310 --> 21:52.644
There's nothing wrong.

21:53.812 --> 21:55.397
The baby's fine, right?

21:56.148 --> 21:58.608
Yes. Her heart's beating well,
and everything looks good.

21:58.692 --> 22:01.278
You have your regular checkup
in three days.

22:01.361 --> 22:04.573
We'll take another look that day,
so there's no need to come until then.

22:04.656 --> 22:06.283
I made sure and checked thoroughly.

22:07.659 --> 22:08.618
Thank you.

22:09.244 --> 22:10.245
Of course.

22:27.304 --> 22:28.430
Did you wait long?

22:28.513 --> 22:29.848
I had a lot to wrap up.

22:29.931 --> 22:31.850
No, I just finished and came down now.

22:31.933 --> 22:33.268
You're right on time.

22:34.478 --> 22:37.481
I mean, I could've gone alone,
but Seung-won kept insisting.

22:39.191 --> 22:40.650
They made chicken soup today.

22:40.734 --> 22:42.652
It's not even close to chobok yet though.

22:44.279 --> 22:46.156
Maybe they want to help
replenish our stamina.

22:46.239 --> 22:47.157
Not ours.

22:49.326 --> 22:51.411
Your sister had
her egg retrieval this morning.

22:52.245 --> 22:53.288
That was today?

22:55.082 --> 22:56.541
Geez, Joo-young.

22:56.625 --> 22:58.251
Why didn't she tell me she was here?

23:00.462 --> 23:02.380
Please input your destination.

23:05.550 --> 23:08.220
Seung-won's pretty nosy too, right?

23:08.303 --> 23:11.348
I could've taken the subway,
but he insisted you give me a ride.

23:11.932 --> 23:13.100
You're so busy though.

23:13.850 --> 23:15.519
It's such a bother, right?

23:15.602 --> 23:16.853
Tell me about it.

23:19.064 --> 23:20.941
Re-routing.

23:21.024 --> 23:23.026
No, no!

23:23.110 --> 23:24.486
Dr. Oh, that's not what I meant!

23:25.070 --> 23:25.946
Dr. Oh, I mean…

23:26.446 --> 23:28.365
I wasn't saying
you were a bother, Yi-young.

23:28.448 --> 23:30.450
I have to review surgery videos,

23:30.534 --> 23:32.202
and I miss your sister.

23:33.411 --> 23:34.579
But I have to come back…

23:34.663 --> 23:35.997
I still have work left…

23:36.081 --> 23:38.166
That's what I meant.

23:38.250 --> 23:39.543
You're mad again, aren't you?

23:40.877 --> 23:42.295
At the hospital,

23:42.379 --> 23:45.549
you're known to be
a very sincere, empathetic,

23:45.632 --> 23:47.008
and understanding person.

23:48.927 --> 23:50.137
But outside,

23:50.762 --> 23:52.347
you're kind of thoughtless.

23:53.098 --> 23:54.224
You just say anything.

23:55.100 --> 23:55.976
And often.

23:57.102 --> 23:58.270
And only to me.

23:59.938 --> 24:02.399
I'm sorry.
I really didn't mean it like that.

24:03.650 --> 24:05.902
I'm going to sleep,
so don't talk to me until we arrive.

24:07.571 --> 24:08.613
You'll bother me.

24:13.118 --> 24:14.119
Let's go.

24:20.167 --> 24:21.835
I'll drive you there safely.

24:29.176 --> 24:31.261
You like music, right?
Should I turn it on?

24:31.344 --> 24:33.471
No, I said I'm going to sleep.

24:34.639 --> 24:36.224
But you still answered.

24:37.100 --> 24:38.727
DR. MYEONG

24:39.477 --> 24:40.896
Why is she calling now?

24:42.022 --> 24:43.273
It's obvious.

24:43.356 --> 24:44.858
She wants to give you more work.

24:46.568 --> 24:47.527
Hello, Doctor.

24:47.611 --> 24:49.988
Dr. Ku, are you okay to talk on the phone?

24:50.071 --> 24:51.948
Yes. Is everything all right
at the hospital?

24:52.032 --> 24:53.617
This isn't about the hospital.

24:53.700 --> 24:56.870
It's about our paper.

24:56.953 --> 24:57.787
Sorry?

24:58.288 --> 24:59.998
The paper we submitted last month.

25:00.081 --> 25:01.249
Right!

25:01.333 --> 25:03.960
After cleaning things up
before submission,

25:04.044 --> 25:06.421
the difference in the level
of contribution seemed too big

25:06.504 --> 25:08.632
for us to be both lead authors.

25:09.466 --> 25:10.926
There were many insufficient parts,

25:11.009 --> 25:13.595
so I had to rewrite a lot of things.

25:13.678 --> 25:14.512
Pardon?

25:14.596 --> 25:19.017
So I put you
as the second author at the end.

25:20.435 --> 25:21.853
I didn't tell you, did I?

25:23.021 --> 25:25.190
Gosh, what's wrong with me?

25:25.273 --> 25:28.276
I should have told you
before I submitted it.

25:29.361 --> 25:30.278
Right?

25:33.198 --> 25:34.032
Hello?

25:36.034 --> 25:37.911
Can you hear me, Dr. Ku?

25:38.495 --> 25:39.412
Yes.

25:39.496 --> 25:40.372
Right.

25:40.914 --> 25:42.999
Dr. Ku, I know you worked hard on this--

25:43.083 --> 25:45.043
Doctor, I'm actually driving right now.

25:45.126 --> 25:47.462
Really? Then--

25:47.545 --> 25:48.964
I'll call you back later.

26:21.913 --> 26:23.748
Do-won, want to drink some soju?

26:27.502 --> 26:29.254
There's beer if you want that instead.

26:36.344 --> 26:37.387
Are you sleeping?

26:56.072 --> 26:57.615
I'll have the six-inch veggie sub.

26:57.699 --> 26:59.909
I'll have it on wheat bread
with American cheese.

26:59.993 --> 27:02.245
Please hold just the onions
and bell peppers.

27:02.329 --> 27:04.456
And I'll have some black pepper
and olive oil on it.

27:04.539 --> 27:05.623
Thank you.

27:07.542 --> 27:10.795
Six-inch steak and cheese
on white bread with shredded cheese

27:10.879 --> 27:12.047
and extra meat, please.

27:12.130 --> 27:13.214
I'll have all the veggies.

27:13.298 --> 27:15.342
And I'd like the ranch
and sweet onion sauce.

27:16.092 --> 27:17.093
Extra sauce, please.

27:19.054 --> 27:20.680
They even have opposite tastes.

27:22.057 --> 27:25.143
I'll have this month's sandwich
with everything on it.

27:25.226 --> 27:27.228
I'll take whatever bread
and sauce is recommended.

27:28.730 --> 27:29.731
And it's a six-inch sub.

27:31.775 --> 27:33.109
I'll have the same as him.

27:35.070 --> 27:36.821
But make mine a footlong, please.

27:41.409 --> 27:43.536
HONG GI-DONG
DON'T CALL ME THIS TIME

27:46.498 --> 27:48.041
Tonight at 9:30 p.m. at Yoon's Cafe.

27:48.833 --> 27:50.752
If you don't show, it's over for real.

27:57.425 --> 27:58.843
Man, I'm hungry.

28:01.221 --> 28:02.764
You're clocking in and not out, right?

28:03.598 --> 28:04.766
You all look so shabby.

28:05.809 --> 28:07.435
You're the worst, okay?

28:08.144 --> 28:10.021
How many days
have you worn those same clothes?

28:10.105 --> 28:11.022
Three days.

28:13.900 --> 28:14.984
It's time to go home.

28:15.068 --> 28:15.902
You probably can't.

28:16.403 --> 28:17.695
You make the study materials?

28:17.779 --> 28:19.697
No. When's that due?

28:19.781 --> 28:22.534
-Tomorrow.
-Really?

28:23.451 --> 28:24.452
Right.

28:24.536 --> 28:27.330
Did you send the research
progress update to Professor Seo?

28:27.414 --> 28:28.248
No.

28:28.331 --> 28:30.708
Damn it. I'll never have time to do that.

28:30.792 --> 28:32.335
I sent mine!

28:32.419 --> 28:34.546
I'm leaving work on time
no matter what today.

28:35.338 --> 28:36.548
You can't.

28:36.631 --> 28:38.425
You have to organize data
for Dr. Jo's paper.

28:39.342 --> 28:40.427
You're right.

28:40.510 --> 28:42.262
And we have plenty of other work too.

28:42.804 --> 28:44.264
I already looked into it yesterday.

28:44.347 --> 28:46.850
This morning, we have
two multi and primi inductions each.

28:46.933 --> 28:49.269
All delivery rooms will be full
and we'll have C-sections.

28:49.352 --> 28:52.105
There are fifteen surgeries in GYN today.

28:52.605 --> 28:54.023
Of those, five are debulking.

28:54.816 --> 28:56.192
So eat up.

28:58.319 --> 29:01.740
This might be our last meal today.

29:12.751 --> 29:14.919
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

29:25.430 --> 29:27.140
Congratulations, Dr. Myeong.

29:27.223 --> 29:28.224
You too, Dr. Ku.

29:28.850 --> 29:30.101
Great work.

29:31.311 --> 29:32.979
Sorry? For what?

29:33.062 --> 29:35.356
You were listed as a presenter
for the conference.

29:38.610 --> 29:41.362
What, were you going to surprise him?
You still haven't told him?

29:41.946 --> 29:44.365
What's wrong with me these days?
I forgot again.

29:45.408 --> 29:47.452
We were selected to present our paper.

29:47.535 --> 29:49.204
I just got the email a few days ago.

29:49.996 --> 29:52.290
It's all thanks to your help, Professor.

29:52.373 --> 29:53.583
Thank you.

29:53.666 --> 29:54.501
Bullshit.

29:54.584 --> 29:56.336
Since you're presenting second,

29:56.419 --> 29:57.962
I smell a possible award.

29:58.671 --> 30:00.381
I guess you'll be presenting, Dr. Myeong?

30:00.465 --> 30:01.633
You're the lead author.

30:01.716 --> 30:04.135
Yes, I'll do my best to prepare.

30:05.929 --> 30:07.931
Dr. Myeong told me.

30:08.014 --> 30:10.266
If you hadn't been busy at the end,

30:10.350 --> 30:12.894
you would've been co-lead authors.

30:12.977 --> 30:14.229
That's too bad.

30:15.730 --> 30:16.815
Well…

30:16.898 --> 30:18.233
I'm sure I'll get other chances.

30:19.150 --> 30:19.984
Goodness!

30:20.735 --> 30:22.612
It was worth being a corresponding author.

30:22.695 --> 30:24.656
I don't think Jung-min's paper got in.

30:25.448 --> 30:27.492
Ms. Cha in Room 6104's bleeding!

30:46.261 --> 30:48.346
It's acute bleeding
caused by placenta previa.

30:48.429 --> 30:51.140
Labor has started,
so we'll go into surgery now.

30:51.224 --> 30:53.226
What about the baby? Is it okay?

30:53.309 --> 30:54.769
It's fine.

30:55.937 --> 30:57.814
Crossmatch and prep three units of blood.

30:57.897 --> 30:59.107
Bring one universal O blood.

30:59.190 --> 31:00.066
Yes, ma'am.

31:00.149 --> 31:01.985
Dr. Oh, inform the guardian.

31:02.068 --> 31:02.902
Yes, ma'am.

31:03.486 --> 31:04.863
Where is your husband now?

31:04.946 --> 31:06.531
He went to buy shoes.

31:07.115 --> 31:09.242
It'll take him 30 minutes to get here.

31:09.325 --> 31:10.326
What do we do?

31:20.420 --> 31:22.547
Has the surgery started?
It's supposed to be tomorrow.

31:22.630 --> 31:25.133
There was sudden acute bleeding
with labor pains.

31:25.216 --> 31:26.593
We have to take the baby out now.

31:26.676 --> 31:28.469
Your wife's in surgery now.

31:29.095 --> 31:30.388
Will they be okay?

31:30.471 --> 31:32.265
My wife and baby?

31:32.348 --> 31:35.435
The professor arrived early
and is monitoring her now.

31:36.728 --> 31:37.562
My goodness.

31:37.645 --> 31:39.480
Why did I buy these?
I couldn't see her off.

31:39.564 --> 31:40.982
As we explained before,

31:41.065 --> 31:42.567
something could suddenly happen,

31:42.650 --> 31:43.860
so please stay near your room.

31:43.943 --> 31:47.280
-Don't stray too far.
-Yes, I won't move an inch from here.

31:48.489 --> 31:49.866
Doctor, wait.

31:50.533 --> 31:51.618
Please take care of her.

31:51.701 --> 31:54.329
Please take good care of my baby.

31:54.412 --> 31:56.122
-I will.
-Thank you.

31:56.205 --> 31:57.373
Please go in.

32:00.710 --> 32:01.794
Oh, God.

32:06.299 --> 32:07.175
Going home?

32:08.051 --> 32:10.303
Yes, for the first time in three days.

32:11.763 --> 32:12.722
Right.

32:12.805 --> 32:15.058
Wash up and get some rest tonight.

32:15.975 --> 32:17.101
I will.

32:17.185 --> 32:18.061
See you tomorrow.

32:18.144 --> 32:19.520
Good night.

32:21.356 --> 32:23.816
MS. TAE-RIM

32:24.609 --> 32:25.610
Yes, ma'am?

32:26.527 --> 32:27.528
Of course, I'll be there.

32:28.655 --> 32:29.656
I'm at the hospital.

32:31.282 --> 32:33.368
Who goes home at this hour?

32:36.746 --> 32:38.498
Does your stomach feel tight again?

32:38.581 --> 32:39.916
Since when has it felt this way?

32:41.125 --> 32:42.585
This morning.

32:43.920 --> 32:45.964
This time, it feels tight all over.

32:46.547 --> 32:47.632
I see.

32:50.343 --> 32:51.344
Ms. Moon.

32:52.428 --> 32:53.638
Everything is fine.

32:54.263 --> 32:55.473
So there's nothing to look at.

32:56.349 --> 32:57.558
Nothing's wrong?

32:57.642 --> 32:59.143
Yes, nothing at all.

32:59.769 --> 33:01.270
You can go home.

33:01.354 --> 33:03.982
We'll see you on Saturday
at your regular checkup.

33:14.951 --> 33:17.495
She didn't take as much time today.

33:18.121 --> 33:20.498
She checked the heart
and amniotic fluid, right?

33:20.581 --> 33:21.791
Yes.

33:21.874 --> 33:24.961
She can read an ultrasound
with her eyes closed.

33:25.044 --> 33:27.380
She checked everything precisely.

33:30.383 --> 33:32.385
Sorry, but I was wondering…

33:36.055 --> 33:37.432
If it's okay with you,

33:38.016 --> 33:39.350
would you like me to take a look?

33:40.143 --> 33:41.019
What?

33:41.102 --> 33:44.397
I'm not as good as her,

33:44.480 --> 33:46.774
but fortunately, I really take my time.

33:47.358 --> 33:50.361
So, I'm an expert
at reading things slowly,

33:50.445 --> 33:52.989
and my specialty is checking
everything multiple times.

33:54.532 --> 33:56.159
If it's not too much for you,

33:56.242 --> 33:59.871
would you like me to take a look
at the area where it feels tight?

34:00.788 --> 34:02.832
I'd be grateful.

34:04.083 --> 34:06.335
Actually, I've wanted to try this,

34:06.419 --> 34:08.254
so I've been hovering around here.

34:08.838 --> 34:11.716
For us,
this is a great opportunity to learn.

34:12.550 --> 34:13.426
All right.

34:15.219 --> 34:18.431
Still, among the first-years,
when it comes to ultrasounds,

34:18.514 --> 34:19.932
I've done it the most.

34:20.016 --> 34:21.726
-Right?
-Yes, he's right.

34:22.435 --> 34:24.103
So, please don't worry.

34:25.313 --> 34:26.397
Okay.

34:29.984 --> 34:31.652
Here's the head.

34:32.236 --> 34:34.489
This is the baby's eyes, nose,

34:34.572 --> 34:36.074
and mouth.

34:36.157 --> 34:37.200
Okay…

34:38.451 --> 34:39.827
The baby's kicking.

34:41.537 --> 34:42.538
Soccer's in the cards.

34:44.415 --> 34:45.833
I'll let you hear the heartbeat.

34:46.334 --> 34:47.168
Okay.

34:53.174 --> 34:54.550
The heart's beating strong.

34:56.094 --> 34:56.969
Right.

35:03.017 --> 35:05.603
-Doctor, can we get the oxytocin now?
-Yes, ma'am.

35:08.523 --> 35:09.899
How's the baby?

35:10.566 --> 35:11.734
Yes, the baby's doing fine.

35:12.735 --> 35:14.987
Placenta adhesion's more severe
than expected.

35:15.696 --> 35:16.656
Dr. Oh, this side too.

35:17.323 --> 35:18.157
Yes, sir.

35:24.247 --> 35:26.040
Tell the intervention team from Radiology

35:26.124 --> 35:28.251
and Dr. Ryu
about the situation in advance.

35:28.334 --> 35:29.418
Yes, ma'am.

35:29.502 --> 35:30.795
-Yi-young.
-Yes?

35:30.878 --> 35:32.630
We'll need consent.

35:32.713 --> 35:35.967
Embolization and hysterectomy.
Tell him we may have to do both. Hurry.

35:36.050 --> 35:37.051
Yes, ma'am.

35:39.637 --> 35:41.013
Is the uterine balloon ready?

35:41.097 --> 35:42.515
Yes, it's ready.

35:42.598 --> 35:43.558
BP's dropping.

35:43.641 --> 35:45.434
-More gauze, please.
-Yes.

35:46.018 --> 35:48.729
There are ten fingers and toes.

35:48.813 --> 35:50.022
The baby's breathing well too.

35:50.106 --> 35:51.315
Congratulations.

35:51.399 --> 35:52.692
Congratulations, sir.

35:52.775 --> 35:55.111
We'll take the baby to the newborn unit.

35:56.445 --> 35:57.530
Thank you.

36:09.876 --> 36:11.127
We're removing the placenta,

36:11.210 --> 36:13.045
but severe adhesion's
causing heavy bleeding.

36:13.838 --> 36:14.755
As we said before--

36:14.839 --> 36:16.174
No, not my wife.

36:16.799 --> 36:18.509
No, I don't want to do it. Please.

36:18.593 --> 36:21.345
We'll insert the balloon.
If it doesn't work, we'll do embolization.

36:21.429 --> 36:23.097
If it worsens, we may do a hysterectomy.

36:23.723 --> 36:25.808
We explained this before. Do you remember?

36:26.434 --> 36:28.561
Is it really bad? How bad is it?

36:28.644 --> 36:29.604
There's heavy bleeding.

36:29.687 --> 36:32.607
We don't know what will happen.
That's why I'm telling you.

36:32.690 --> 36:34.483
Then let me go in for a moment.

36:34.567 --> 36:35.610
Let me just see her.

36:35.693 --> 36:36.569
Sir!

36:36.652 --> 36:38.196
There's no time! You must sign.

36:40.489 --> 36:41.365
Hurry.

36:46.621 --> 36:47.496
Thank you.

36:49.540 --> 36:54.587
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY
EXIT

37:07.183 --> 37:08.142
It's better now, right?

37:08.226 --> 37:09.268
Yes, Professor.

37:09.352 --> 37:11.020
Sir, how are her vitals?

37:11.103 --> 37:13.314
BP is 100 over 60, pulse is 100.

37:13.856 --> 37:15.566
Do-won, let's insert the balloon now.

37:15.650 --> 37:17.068
-Let's try.
-Yes, ma'am.

37:26.786 --> 37:28.913
We don't know yet,
so don't cancel the embolization

37:28.996 --> 37:31.165
or the call Dr. Ryu!

37:31.249 --> 37:32.250
Yes, ma'am.

37:32.333 --> 37:33.834
Inserting the catheter!

37:35.753 --> 37:36.754
I got it.

37:36.837 --> 37:38.089
Do-won, start ballooning.

37:38.172 --> 37:39.006
Yes, ma'am.

37:43.135 --> 37:46.264
INFLATING WITH SALINE
TO APPLY PRESSURE AND STOP BLEEDING

37:48.349 --> 37:49.850
I've administered 50 cc.

37:51.852 --> 37:53.062
I'll administer 50 more.

37:53.145 --> 37:54.397
Do 100 cc more.

37:54.480 --> 37:55.314
Yes, ma'am.

37:59.193 --> 38:00.319
That's a total of 200 cc.

38:01.988 --> 38:03.572
Pack and secure the catheter now.

38:04.365 --> 38:05.616
Yes, ma'am.

38:07.618 --> 38:09.537
The 1-0 suture, please.

38:09.620 --> 38:10.788
1-0 REFERS TO SUTURE SIZE

38:17.712 --> 38:19.380
-Hold it steady.
-Yes, ma'am.

38:20.923 --> 38:23.259
-Hold it right. It's coming loose!
-Yes, ma'am.

38:38.983 --> 38:40.318
We've stopped the bleeding.

38:41.902 --> 38:44.697
Then is my baby okay?
She's not bleeding anymore?

38:44.780 --> 38:47.742
There were uterine contractions,
so the bleeding has stopped.

38:47.825 --> 38:49.535
Fortunately, we didn't remove the uterus,

38:49.618 --> 38:52.121
the balloon worked as intended,
and surgery went well.

38:52.830 --> 38:54.165
Thank you, Doctor.

38:55.041 --> 38:57.043
Thank you.

38:57.793 --> 38:59.628
Since there was severe placental adhesion,

38:59.712 --> 39:01.922
she had multiple transfusions
for heavy bleeding.

39:02.006 --> 39:03.215
It was very rough on her.

39:04.175 --> 39:05.926
Is everything okay now?

39:06.010 --> 39:08.262
There are no problems, right?

39:08.346 --> 39:09.430
She's fine now.

39:10.014 --> 39:11.891
She may start bleeding again,

39:11.974 --> 39:13.559
so we'll monitor her for an hour.

39:13.642 --> 39:15.728
If nothing happens,
she'll return to her room.

39:16.437 --> 39:18.689
Doctor, thank you so much.

39:18.773 --> 39:21.150
Thank you for saving my baby.

39:22.902 --> 39:27.031
Goodness, you seem to have aged overnight.

39:27.573 --> 39:29.450
Your wife will be shocked
when she sees you.

39:31.494 --> 39:33.412
Well, not as shocked as I was.

39:33.496 --> 39:36.040
Seriously, I thought my heart
would pop out of my chest.

39:54.558 --> 39:57.186
TONIGHT AT 9:30 P.M. AT YOON'S CAFE

40:03.192 --> 40:04.151
How much is left?

40:04.235 --> 40:05.361
What?

40:05.444 --> 40:06.946
You're tossing it
to me in 30 minutes.

40:07.613 --> 40:08.614
I'm working on it.

40:12.243 --> 40:15.871
But didn't he say
he just wanted this by today?

40:15.955 --> 40:17.998
Then we can just send it before midnight.

40:18.082 --> 40:18.916
No.

40:19.458 --> 40:22.586
It means he wants to review it today,
so it's due before he leaves.

40:23.379 --> 40:26.340
Dr. Jo usually leaves at 11:00 p.m.,
so it's due before then.

40:27.508 --> 40:30.719
And I need to combine mine with yours,
so we don't have time.

40:30.803 --> 40:32.138
I'm almost done.

40:33.180 --> 40:35.724
Hey, let's just rest for an hour.

40:36.934 --> 40:38.936
I'm just going to go
to Yoon's Cafe out front

40:39.728 --> 40:40.980
and get a coffee.

40:41.063 --> 40:42.273
I had coffee earlier.

40:42.356 --> 40:44.316
I want some. Me.

40:44.400 --> 40:46.610
You said you're almost done.
Just drink it after.

40:51.365 --> 40:52.199
Or,

40:53.451 --> 40:54.493
since I'm done,

40:54.577 --> 40:57.788
you can send it after combining ours
and call Dr. Jo.

40:57.872 --> 40:59.874
No, you said you'd do that.

41:00.624 --> 41:02.793
You've never called him before,
so you don't know,

41:02.877 --> 41:04.462
but he's always cranky on the phone.

41:04.545 --> 41:06.839
-I don't want to call him either.
-Fine!

41:07.715 --> 41:10.092
I'll just do it fast.
I'm doing it right now.

41:10.801 --> 41:11.886
-Do it.
-Okay!

41:21.312 --> 41:22.313
Honey, are you okay?

41:26.484 --> 41:28.027
It must've been so hard.

41:29.195 --> 41:31.489
I missed you so much.

41:32.198 --> 41:34.200
And our little tot's healthy.

41:34.825 --> 41:37.495
She's so beautiful like you.

41:41.248 --> 41:43.501
You'll have some pain from the balloon.

41:44.001 --> 41:45.544
We'll control it with painkillers,

41:45.628 --> 41:47.546
but let us know if it hurts a lot.

41:48.464 --> 41:50.174
We'll remove the balloon in the morning.

41:50.257 --> 41:53.260
And we'll check again
for bleeding after removal.

41:53.344 --> 41:54.178
Okay.

41:55.804 --> 41:58.140
Honey, I'm going to take care of you.

41:58.224 --> 41:59.058
Okay?

42:03.687 --> 42:05.606
Don't worry about anything.

42:07.107 --> 42:08.943
Let's just focus on our second child.

42:10.361 --> 42:13.781
I prayed so hard
for your uterus to not be removed.

42:14.657 --> 42:16.200
We need to have a son.

42:16.283 --> 42:19.036
One daughter and one son.
That was my dream.

42:20.621 --> 42:22.998
Let's rest for two months
and try for a second.

42:23.082 --> 42:24.833
You can do it, my baby.

42:27.586 --> 42:29.213
Excuse me, sir?

42:31.298 --> 42:32.174
Wait…

42:49.692 --> 42:51.944
You f***ing piece of s***.

42:52.861 --> 42:54.697
Have you lost your damn mind?

42:55.197 --> 42:57.783
How can you say that
at a time like this, you son of a b****?

43:06.417 --> 43:09.128
She asked me to deliver that message.

43:09.920 --> 43:12.298
If not, she was going to
leave the hospital.

43:12.381 --> 43:15.092
I mean, but still…

43:16.468 --> 43:17.344
Honey, are you okay?

43:17.428 --> 43:18.762
Are you still out of it?

43:33.027 --> 43:36.071
She wants me to say the rest.

43:41.452 --> 43:42.870
You a**hole!

44:28.082 --> 44:29.917
Dr. Jo said he'd review it
and get back to us.

44:31.168 --> 44:32.294
Aren't you hungry?

44:35.422 --> 44:36.924
We finished sooner than I thought.

44:37.007 --> 44:38.509
It's only 10:30 p.m.

44:39.259 --> 44:40.427
It is?

44:41.887 --> 44:42.971
It's 10:30 p.m.?

44:46.642 --> 44:47.518
What?

44:48.852 --> 44:49.937
He read it.

44:50.020 --> 44:52.106
Gi-dong read it.

44:53.107 --> 44:54.149
Wait, when did he read it?

44:54.233 --> 44:55.818
He hadn't earlier.

44:57.152 --> 44:58.320
It's past 9:30 p.m., right?

44:58.987 --> 45:00.030
Yeah, it's 10:32 p.m.

45:00.114 --> 45:01.490
Oh, no!

45:01.573 --> 45:03.409
What if he left after waiting?

45:03.492 --> 45:04.785
Who? What?

45:04.868 --> 45:05.911
Forget it.

45:06.495 --> 45:07.955
This is all your fault.

45:11.792 --> 45:13.419
What is she talking about?

45:33.480 --> 45:35.899
Did he come? Or did he leave?

45:37.943 --> 45:39.486
Is he mad at me?

45:40.112 --> 45:42.114
HONG GI-DONG

45:44.324 --> 45:49.413
YOON'S CAFE

45:53.250 --> 45:55.544
Dr. Myeong's presentation
is tomorrow, right?

45:55.627 --> 45:57.463
-Yes.
-Which first-year is going?

45:58.964 --> 45:59.798
Oh Yi-young.

46:00.966 --> 46:03.051
Do you have plans,

46:03.135 --> 46:06.013
family obligations,
or a pending illness again?

46:07.514 --> 46:08.891
You've never gone to a conference.

46:08.974 --> 46:10.934
You know it's a requirement
for residency, right?

46:11.018 --> 46:11.894
When will you go?

46:12.561 --> 46:13.729
I'll go next time.

46:13.812 --> 46:15.189
Go to this one. That's an order.

46:16.231 --> 46:17.107
You're going, right?

46:17.191 --> 46:18.025
Sorry?

46:18.108 --> 46:19.776
The second author should be there.

46:19.860 --> 46:20.819
It's a happy day.

46:21.987 --> 46:24.364
Okay. I'll go with Dr. Oh.

46:24.448 --> 46:25.282
Good.

46:25.365 --> 46:27.367
You both worked hard. Have some good food.

46:27.451 --> 46:29.077
Have a drink too!

46:29.161 --> 46:29.995
Yes, ma'am.

46:37.920 --> 46:39.630
We've removed the balloon and kept watch.

46:39.713 --> 46:42.257
There is no bleeding at all.
It's great news.

46:42.341 --> 46:44.384
Yes, thank you.

46:44.468 --> 46:47.095
But where's your husband today?

46:48.972 --> 46:51.433
He's very popular in this ward.

46:51.517 --> 46:53.685
Everyone's so jealous of you.

46:53.769 --> 46:55.521
They all wish to be in your shoes.

46:57.231 --> 47:00.025
Everyone said, "He's so sweet."

47:00.108 --> 47:02.694
So I thought "So Sweet" was his name.

47:05.197 --> 47:08.617
I couldn't stand the sight of him
and sent him home.

47:08.700 --> 47:10.285
He won't be coming for a while.

47:11.119 --> 47:12.871
What? Why?

47:13.622 --> 47:15.624
Such caring husbands like him
are hard to come by.

47:16.667 --> 47:19.044
Is he too clingy?
Too outwardly expressive?

47:19.127 --> 47:20.295
And you don't like that.

47:20.379 --> 47:21.630
Gosh.

47:21.713 --> 47:22.548
-Still--
-Professor?

47:23.173 --> 47:25.634
Ms. Han in Room 6107 is waiting.

47:25.717 --> 47:28.554
She believes your words
like the gospel itself.

47:28.637 --> 47:30.222
I'm sure she's been waiting since dawn.

47:30.305 --> 47:31.306
We should get going.

47:31.390 --> 47:33.392
Right, she must've waited
a long time for me.

47:33.475 --> 47:34.393
Let's go.

47:34.476 --> 47:35.310
Goodbye!

47:50.158 --> 47:51.743
This is Um Jae-il from OB-GYN.

47:53.495 --> 47:55.330
Today's…

47:56.456 --> 47:59.001
It's Saturday, so I'm resting.

47:59.918 --> 48:03.088
A patient's asking for you.
I called to see if you were available.

48:04.548 --> 48:05.882
Ma'am.

48:06.842 --> 48:08.802
I'm going to say no just for today.

48:09.595 --> 48:11.722
-Just once.
-Okay.

48:11.805 --> 48:13.599
I'll call Dr. Oh instead.

48:13.682 --> 48:14.516
Get some rest.

48:16.184 --> 48:17.019
Wait.

48:17.102 --> 48:17.936
But…

48:18.562 --> 48:19.605
She's asking for me?

48:20.731 --> 48:22.316
Someone's asking for me?

48:28.488 --> 48:30.741
Were there any unique symptoms
yesterday or today?

48:31.783 --> 48:32.826
No.

48:34.995 --> 48:38.165
Today's my scheduled
outpatient appointment.

48:38.707 --> 48:40.167
I didn't just come.

48:41.168 --> 48:42.044
I know.

48:42.586 --> 48:46.423
Please be thorough like last time, Doctor.

48:46.506 --> 48:48.884
Yes, I'll do my best.

48:52.054 --> 48:54.222
The baby's heartbeat is strong.

48:54.306 --> 48:55.807
It's moving well too.

48:56.558 --> 48:59.144
The amniotic fluid level is also normal.

49:00.187 --> 49:01.563
And…

49:10.322 --> 49:11.156
What is it?

49:12.532 --> 49:14.034
Is something wrong?

49:15.327 --> 49:16.870
-Ms. Tae-rim?
-Yes?

49:16.953 --> 49:18.246
Please alert the professor.

49:18.872 --> 49:19.706
What?

49:20.749 --> 49:21.667
I'm not sure.

49:21.750 --> 49:23.502
But I see something like a blood vessel.

49:24.670 --> 49:26.213
Please tell her she needs to see it.

49:27.339 --> 49:28.465
Okay.

49:38.350 --> 49:40.352
This isn't something easy to find.

49:43.230 --> 49:46.066
Jae-il, this is a uterine rupture.

49:47.150 --> 49:48.193
That's…

49:49.778 --> 49:50.904
Ms. Moon.

49:50.987 --> 49:53.824
We're looking at the umbilical cord now.

49:53.907 --> 49:54.741
Okay.

49:54.825 --> 49:56.702
Along with the amniotic sac,

49:56.785 --> 49:59.037
the cord is slightly protruding

49:59.121 --> 50:00.706
outside the uterine wall.

50:01.540 --> 50:03.625
Luckily, the amniotic sac hasn't ruptured.

50:03.709 --> 50:05.585
What does that mean?

50:05.669 --> 50:08.880
I think it would be best
to deliver the baby via surgery.

50:08.964 --> 50:09.881
What?

50:09.965 --> 50:11.383
Should I prep the OR?

50:11.466 --> 50:13.176
Yeah. Someone should be wrapping up.

50:14.136 --> 50:15.178
Okay.

50:16.722 --> 50:18.348
While we prep for surgery,

50:18.432 --> 50:21.351
you'll stay in the delivery room,
so we'll transfer you soon.

50:21.852 --> 50:22.853
Don't be alarmed.

50:25.272 --> 50:27.774
The baby's not in danger, right?

50:28.692 --> 50:30.152
Everything's fine. Right, Professor?

50:30.235 --> 50:32.988
We're doing the surgery
so the baby will be fine.

50:34.156 --> 50:35.991
Don't you worry.

50:36.950 --> 50:38.452
You can put your trust in me.

50:50.046 --> 50:50.881
Yes, Professor?

50:52.174 --> 50:53.008
What?

50:53.675 --> 50:55.510
There's no way any data's missing.

50:56.678 --> 50:58.221
Nam-kyung did that part.

51:01.183 --> 51:02.726
We should have checked one last time.

51:02.809 --> 51:03.643
I'm sorry.

51:04.478 --> 51:06.146
We'll fix it and send it back…

51:12.694 --> 51:14.029
Geez, Nam-kyung.

51:16.948 --> 51:17.824
Eat up.

51:17.908 --> 51:19.075
Hello.

51:27.334 --> 51:28.335
What is it now?

51:29.169 --> 51:30.378
Dr. Ku.

51:30.462 --> 51:32.756
I've never fought with anyone in my life.

51:33.340 --> 51:35.967
But that's all I'm doing these days.

51:36.718 --> 51:37.719
With who?

51:40.096 --> 51:41.890
I don't think I should reveal who it is.

51:43.183 --> 51:45.894
Not talking about people behind their back
is my work life rule.

51:47.813 --> 51:48.647
All right.

51:49.356 --> 51:50.232
What's the issue?

51:50.315 --> 51:51.691
I just don't get them.

51:51.775 --> 51:53.652
What they say and how they act and think.

51:53.735 --> 51:56.488
Trying to talk to understand them
just makes things worse.

51:57.197 --> 51:58.782
I have no idea what to do.

51:59.866 --> 52:00.700
Want me to tell you?

52:04.204 --> 52:05.372
Don't try to understand.

52:06.540 --> 52:08.792
Just accept that's how they are. Okay?

52:09.626 --> 52:12.587
Taking issue with everything
to understand them won't change anything.

52:13.630 --> 52:16.049
You can leave someone behind,
but you can't fix them.

52:16.633 --> 52:19.678
Wasting your energy and time
on something that won't ever improve

52:19.761 --> 52:22.305
is only a loss for you in the end,
so why do it?

52:26.726 --> 52:29.563
Still, I think I need to
talk it over with them.

52:30.856 --> 52:33.483
Whether I can fix them or not
is not my problem.

52:34.317 --> 52:35.652
I have to speak my mind.

52:36.152 --> 52:39.155
I was the one negatively affected.
Why should I tolerate it too?

52:39.948 --> 52:41.032
I can't do that.

52:48.707 --> 52:50.709
The baby is fine.

52:50.792 --> 52:52.711
At 2.3 kilograms,

52:52.794 --> 52:54.504
she's small for the gestational age.

52:54.588 --> 52:57.883
But her heart rate,
breathing, and movement

52:57.966 --> 52:58.842
are all good.

53:00.260 --> 53:03.513
I've done so many ultrasounds.

53:05.140 --> 53:06.474
Well…

53:06.558 --> 53:09.978
I've reviewed all
the previous ultrasounds,

53:10.061 --> 53:11.688
and there were no issues.

53:11.771 --> 53:14.691
Even if you get an ultrasound daily,

53:14.774 --> 53:17.277
this is something that can come up

53:17.360 --> 53:19.738
at any time in between.

53:21.114 --> 53:22.157
I don't mean that.

53:23.408 --> 53:27.245
I've done so many ultrasounds.

53:28.121 --> 53:29.706
I'd say I was in pain

53:30.498 --> 53:32.208
and lie every time.

53:33.835 --> 53:38.131
When I'd read online
about bad things happening to babies,

53:38.673 --> 53:41.843
it felt like I was getting
those same symptoms.

53:42.427 --> 53:46.097
And I'd suddenly start
to feel pain that wasn't there.

53:46.681 --> 53:48.266
I know it wasn't true.

53:48.350 --> 53:49.768
But if I didn't get it checked,

53:51.645 --> 53:53.396
I kept thinking bad thoughts.

53:54.105 --> 53:55.106
I'm sorry.

53:55.607 --> 53:59.736
I know you all had a hard time
because of me.

53:59.819 --> 54:01.363
I apologize.

54:01.446 --> 54:02.572
It's all right.

54:02.656 --> 54:04.157
It's completely understandable.

54:04.240 --> 54:07.285
More so
because it was your first pregnancy.

54:07.369 --> 54:08.870
This all happened

54:09.663 --> 54:11.331
because of me.

54:12.082 --> 54:14.000
I even made my baby feel anxious,

54:14.084 --> 54:16.378
so something bad happened inside.

54:16.461 --> 54:19.172
As I told you, that's not the case.

54:19.756 --> 54:22.133
The baby is healthy. Please don't worry.

54:24.719 --> 54:27.430
Our baby was born a week early.

54:28.807 --> 54:29.933
Is it really okay?

54:30.016 --> 54:30.892
Yes.

54:31.434 --> 54:34.229
The baby didn't go
to the neonatal intensive care unit.

54:34.312 --> 54:35.814
It's in the nursery.

54:35.897 --> 54:37.357
I read that if they're born early,

54:37.941 --> 54:40.068
they'll develop problems with their lungs.

54:41.152 --> 54:43.196
Is that likely?

54:43.279 --> 54:45.323
The baby's lungs have fully matured.

54:45.407 --> 54:48.076
And we've run all the checks.

54:48.159 --> 54:49.869
There's nothing to worry about.

54:49.953 --> 54:52.205
You said she's a bit small.

54:52.288 --> 54:54.207
It's not enough to raise concern.

54:54.874 --> 54:56.001
She's fine.

54:56.626 --> 54:57.669
Then…

55:00.505 --> 55:03.008
Can I finally relax now?

55:05.051 --> 55:08.596
Now that my baby's born healthy,

55:10.181 --> 55:12.308
can I live without worrying anymore?

55:13.727 --> 55:15.729
No, you can't.

55:20.358 --> 55:22.193
You must've thought the birth was the end.

55:22.277 --> 55:23.611
It's only the beginning.

55:26.906 --> 55:30.994
My mother turned 70 this year.

55:31.870 --> 55:34.372
She still calls every morning
out of concern.

55:35.957 --> 55:38.293
"Cold water in the morning
will hurt your stomach."

55:38.376 --> 55:40.587
"You'll get into an accident
if you drive at night."

55:41.546 --> 55:43.798
"Don't go out when it rains."

55:45.008 --> 55:47.594
I thought my mom was such a fussy person.

55:48.636 --> 55:51.431
But I'm doing the same thing
to my daughter.

55:54.350 --> 55:56.478
She's in middle school now.

55:56.561 --> 55:58.730
Yesterday, she told me her ankle was sore.

55:59.814 --> 56:01.524
When I heard that, I thought,

56:01.608 --> 56:03.359
"Is it an issue with her muscular tissue?"

56:03.443 --> 56:04.611
"Is it her bone?"

56:05.278 --> 56:08.490
I was so worried, it kept me up at night.

56:08.573 --> 56:11.493
But this morning,
she rode her bike to school and was fine.

56:13.745 --> 56:16.873
There are more things
to worry about after the birth.

56:17.499 --> 56:20.835
So don't hope
that your worries will disappear.

56:23.004 --> 56:25.340
That's much better
for a mother's mental health.

56:26.508 --> 56:30.011
Think of it as the price you pay
for the happiness

56:30.095 --> 56:31.513
that children bring.

56:32.347 --> 56:33.431
What else can you do?

56:34.516 --> 56:35.975
Still, the good thing is

56:36.559 --> 56:39.979
that most of the things
I worry about never happen.

56:43.483 --> 56:44.651
Trust me.

56:45.485 --> 56:47.904
I will. Thank you.

56:52.158 --> 56:53.743
Honey, I brought it.

56:55.787 --> 56:58.540
Where did that doctor go?

56:59.290 --> 57:01.251
The one who read my ultrasound?

57:01.876 --> 57:03.545
He's the best ultrasound reader

57:04.087 --> 57:06.005
in this hospital.

57:10.176 --> 57:11.511
Where did he go?

57:16.474 --> 57:17.559
Dr. Um?

57:19.561 --> 57:21.438
-Hello!
-Nice seeing you here.

57:21.521 --> 57:23.273
How's tennis?

57:23.356 --> 57:25.108
I haven't been able to go for three weeks.

57:25.191 --> 57:27.652
Me neither. I've been so busy these days.

57:27.735 --> 57:28.736
Right?

57:29.237 --> 57:30.905
First-years don't have time for hobbies.

57:31.448 --> 57:32.657
They can barely eat and sleep.

57:33.241 --> 57:34.242
I've been there. I know.

57:34.909 --> 57:35.869
You're working so hard.

57:37.579 --> 57:39.122
But what brings you here?

57:39.205 --> 57:41.166
A baby needed a CS consult.

57:41.249 --> 57:42.167
You?

57:42.250 --> 57:43.835
A mother was worried about her baby.

57:44.711 --> 57:46.880
I came to take a photo to show her.

57:47.547 --> 57:49.299
But they're so cute I can't leave.

57:51.259 --> 57:54.971
I've known this one since the ultrasounds.

57:55.054 --> 57:57.390
And its umbilical cord
was the first one I ever cut.

58:00.310 --> 58:03.229
Oh, right. About ten minutes after birth,

58:03.313 --> 58:05.565
the baby's oxygen saturation was only 90%.

58:05.648 --> 58:06.649
Is that okay?

58:06.733 --> 58:07.859
That's normal.

58:08.693 --> 58:09.527
That's a relief.

58:10.570 --> 58:13.448
Don't you know oxygen saturation
changes by the minute after birth?

58:14.282 --> 58:16.534
Even 85% is normal after ten minutes.

58:18.328 --> 58:21.039
We learn this in med school.
Did you forget all that?

58:21.956 --> 58:22.790
Yes.

58:22.874 --> 58:24.918
That won't do, Dr. Um.

58:25.627 --> 58:26.503
Sir?

58:27.462 --> 58:28.338
All right, then.

58:29.255 --> 58:30.632
A baby that was doing fine

58:30.715 --> 58:33.468
suddenly turns blue
without any other symptoms.

58:33.551 --> 58:34.719
What do you do?

58:39.516 --> 58:40.600
No.

58:41.476 --> 58:43.728
Check the oxygen saturation of the limbs.

58:44.896 --> 58:45.980
Right.

58:46.064 --> 58:46.898
I got it, sir.

58:46.981 --> 58:49.359
Then, if a baby that was fine

58:49.442 --> 58:50.860
suddenly shows cyanosis,

58:50.944 --> 58:52.320
what tests should be done?

58:56.783 --> 58:59.744
An echocardiogram. Right?

59:00.286 --> 59:02.497
You have to check
for a congenital heart defect.

59:04.499 --> 59:05.500
Right.

59:06.000 --> 59:07.210
I'm sorry.

59:10.755 --> 59:11.631
My bad.

59:12.465 --> 59:14.634
We don't have any first-years in CS.

59:15.385 --> 59:17.845
I've always wanted
to quiz my juniors like this.

59:20.390 --> 59:22.308
But where's your baby?

59:23.518 --> 59:25.812
The smallest one at the end there.

59:27.146 --> 59:29.274
She's the shortest

59:29.357 --> 59:31.025
and weighs the least.

59:31.609 --> 59:32.777
She's in last place here.

59:36.948 --> 59:38.157
Who cares if she is?

59:39.784 --> 59:41.286
That doesn't matter right now.

59:42.078 --> 59:43.788
She can be in first place when she leaves.

59:47.834 --> 59:49.335
It's the first day of her life.

59:50.336 --> 59:51.713
She's only getting started.

01:00:01.973 --> 01:00:04.892
They said pain can persist
for a week after the egg retrieval.

01:00:08.271 --> 01:00:10.440
I'm fine.
There was no fluid buildup this time.

01:00:16.946 --> 01:00:19.032
If the hospital calls, I'll tell you.

01:00:44.849 --> 01:00:47.060
FERTILITY CENTER

01:00:48.811 --> 01:00:50.396
Hello, Doctor.

01:00:52.523 --> 01:00:54.275
How did it go? How many are there?

01:00:54.859 --> 01:00:57.654
The day after egg retrieval,
two eggs were fertilized,

01:00:57.737 --> 01:00:58.863
and as we explained before,

01:00:58.946 --> 01:01:01.741
they were cultured
for a five-day embryo transfer…

01:01:03.660 --> 01:01:05.995
But both embryos
weren't in good condition,

01:01:06.079 --> 01:01:07.497
and it was unsuccessful.

01:01:08.164 --> 01:01:09.582
I'm sure you must be disappointed,

01:01:10.416 --> 01:01:13.586
but embryo transfer
won't be possible this time.

01:01:18.341 --> 01:01:19.258
Excuse me.

01:01:50.123 --> 01:01:52.750
Did you wait long? Are you mad?

01:01:53.334 --> 01:01:55.670
Please pick up.

01:01:55.753 --> 01:01:56.921
Hey!

01:01:58.047 --> 01:02:00.383
I'm sorry.

01:02:12.520 --> 01:02:13.396
What now?

01:02:15.648 --> 01:02:17.442
Let's do it tomorrow, okay?

01:02:17.525 --> 01:02:18.860
What?

01:02:18.943 --> 01:02:20.153
Whatever you're going to say,

01:02:21.154 --> 01:02:23.322
I'm not in the mood to talk or fight.

01:02:23.406 --> 01:02:25.116
It's something I have to tell you.

01:02:26.242 --> 01:02:27.160
Fine.

01:02:27.243 --> 01:02:29.120
You just have to say
what you want, don't you?

01:02:29.203 --> 01:02:32.707
The professor saw the data we organized
and gave us feedback.

01:02:32.790 --> 01:02:34.625
You omitted about ten people.

01:02:35.209 --> 01:02:37.253
So I added all of them and sent it back.

01:02:37.837 --> 01:02:40.631
Fine. I wasn't fully focused.

01:02:40.715 --> 01:02:42.675
Okay? Thanks.

01:02:42.759 --> 01:02:43.676
Happy?

01:02:47.054 --> 01:02:49.265
This next one's
about the ward out patient.

01:02:49.348 --> 01:02:52.310
If they arrive at 6:30 p.m.,
it's right that you do it.

01:02:53.978 --> 01:02:54.937
But…

01:02:55.646 --> 01:02:58.441
I had no idea the professor
would get so angry about that.

01:02:59.567 --> 01:03:00.735
Rather than arguing,

01:03:00.818 --> 01:03:02.737
if I had gone to the patient
and explained,

01:03:02.820 --> 01:03:04.363
you wouldn't have been yelled at.

01:03:06.991 --> 01:03:09.452
I'm sorry about that.

01:03:11.245 --> 01:03:12.246
What?

01:03:13.623 --> 01:03:15.291
What's with you all of a sudden?

01:03:15.374 --> 01:03:17.043
Just go back to how you normally are.

01:03:17.752 --> 01:03:19.504
The facts need to be clearly pointed out.

01:03:20.087 --> 01:03:22.757
Whose fault it is
and who should apologize.

01:03:24.675 --> 01:03:26.010
It's a principle of mine.

01:03:29.931 --> 01:03:31.390
I've said my piece.

01:03:33.893 --> 01:03:35.728
Well, I'm…

01:03:38.606 --> 01:03:39.482
sorry too.

01:03:41.192 --> 01:03:43.110
What I said about you to Ms. Yeom,

01:03:43.778 --> 01:03:46.656
about how inflexible you are
and how we're incompatible,

01:03:47.448 --> 01:03:49.200
I didn't mean to talk behind your back.

01:03:49.283 --> 01:03:50.868
I was just venting.

01:03:51.452 --> 01:03:53.788
And as I kept going, I exaggerated a bit.

01:03:56.791 --> 01:03:57.667
I'm sorry.

01:04:01.671 --> 01:04:03.005
I'm done now too.

01:04:07.134 --> 01:04:09.887
So we're all good now, okay?

01:04:15.351 --> 01:04:16.727
That was about me?

01:04:17.395 --> 01:04:18.271
What?

01:04:19.188 --> 01:04:20.147
Not Yi-young?

01:04:21.524 --> 01:04:22.441
It was me?

01:04:22.525 --> 01:04:23.609
What?

01:04:25.194 --> 01:04:26.445
You know,

01:04:26.529 --> 01:04:27.864
talking about another doctor

01:04:27.947 --> 01:04:30.283
in a personal conversation
with a patient is rude.

01:04:31.492 --> 01:04:35.413
And I can't accept the fact
you think I'm inflexible.

01:04:35.496 --> 01:04:37.790
-Why? When? Doing what?
-Sa-bi, eat some squid.

01:04:37.874 --> 01:04:39.542
What were the circumstances?

01:04:39.625 --> 01:04:41.419
-I got a call. Hello?
-When was I inflexible?

01:04:41.502 --> 01:04:42.920
Your phone's upside down.

01:04:43.004 --> 01:04:44.171
-Say something.
-Hello?

01:04:44.255 --> 01:04:45.214
-Hang up.
-Wait.

01:04:45.298 --> 01:04:46.757
-Hang up now.
-Wait, I have to go.

01:04:46.841 --> 01:04:47.800
I'm talking to you.

01:04:48.509 --> 01:04:49.802
The best presentation award

01:04:49.886 --> 01:04:52.555
goes to Dr. Myeong Eun-won
of Jongno Yulje Medical Center.

01:04:52.638 --> 01:04:54.098
To Myeong Eun-won,

01:04:54.724 --> 01:04:56.934
for researching the feasibility
of cervical elastography

01:04:57.018 --> 01:04:59.270
in prediction of preterm delivery

01:04:59.353 --> 01:05:01.981
in pregnancies with short cervixes
after progesterone treatment,

01:05:02.064 --> 01:05:03.816
we present you
this best presentation award.

01:05:04.317 --> 01:05:05.484
Congratulations.

01:05:18.748 --> 01:05:19.582
Congratulations.

01:05:19.665 --> 01:05:21.918
KOREAN SOCIETY OF MATERNAL-FETAL MEDICINE
29TH CONFERENCE

01:05:42.605 --> 01:05:44.607
Dr. Ku, just a moment.

01:05:45.900 --> 01:05:47.193
It's not much.

01:05:47.276 --> 01:05:49.528
I think you should take this.

01:05:49.612 --> 01:05:50.863
No, it's all right.

01:05:51.614 --> 01:05:53.366
I want you to have it.

01:05:53.449 --> 01:05:55.117
No, it's really okay.

01:05:57.662 --> 01:05:58.746
It's just…

01:05:59.330 --> 01:06:01.624
I was wondering if you're upset with me.

01:06:01.707 --> 01:06:03.834
You haven't said much
since we talked on the phone.

01:06:04.502 --> 01:06:06.963
You don't mistakenly think
I stole the paper, do you?

01:06:07.046 --> 01:06:08.923
I know you're not like that,
but just in case…

01:06:10.299 --> 01:06:12.843
If the professors heard
any strange rumors,

01:06:13.552 --> 01:06:15.054
it would be embarrassing for us both.

01:06:19.600 --> 01:06:21.060
You don't have to worry about that.

01:06:21.143 --> 01:06:22.853
Thanks, Dr. Ku.

01:06:22.937 --> 01:06:24.939
I'm really reflecting on myself.

01:06:25.022 --> 01:06:27.566
It really was my mistake
for forgetting and not telling you.

01:06:28.651 --> 01:06:29.527
A mistake?

01:06:29.610 --> 01:06:30.945
Yeah, mistake.

01:06:31.529 --> 01:06:32.863
I really forgot.

01:06:34.115 --> 01:06:36.158
I'm not sure
what's wrong with me these days.

01:06:36.242 --> 01:06:38.327
I get you must be very upset.

01:06:38.411 --> 01:06:39.620
I would be too.

01:06:39.704 --> 01:06:41.706
Next time, this won't ever happen again.

01:06:41.789 --> 01:06:43.165
I promise.

01:06:43.749 --> 01:06:45.418
If you're upset, let it go.

01:06:46.127 --> 01:06:47.753
Yeah, if you write a paper next time,

01:06:47.837 --> 01:06:49.338
I'll help you out.

01:06:50.715 --> 01:06:51.924
Really.

01:06:53.217 --> 01:06:54.218
All right.

01:06:54.927 --> 01:06:56.137
I should get going.

01:06:57.847 --> 01:06:58.723
Hello.

01:06:59.390 --> 01:07:00.516
Dr. Oh.

01:07:04.520 --> 01:07:05.396
So…

01:07:06.188 --> 01:07:08.524
I wasn't trying to,

01:07:10.192 --> 01:07:12.194
but I've overheard you twice now.

01:07:13.779 --> 01:07:15.448
It just happened.

01:07:19.285 --> 01:07:20.911
But you never apologized.

01:07:22.079 --> 01:07:22.955
What?

01:07:26.459 --> 01:07:29.462
You didn't apologize.

01:07:35.134 --> 01:07:38.012
I didn't?

01:07:38.095 --> 01:07:38.929
No.

01:07:44.852 --> 01:07:46.312
I'm sorry, Dr. Ku.

01:07:49.482 --> 01:07:50.316
Sorry.

01:07:55.404 --> 01:07:56.572
I should go.

01:08:08.501 --> 01:08:09.335
Let's go home.

01:08:31.315 --> 01:08:32.525
Why did you say that?

01:08:32.608 --> 01:08:34.151
I don't need an apology.

01:08:34.235 --> 01:08:35.736
But I do.

01:08:40.533 --> 01:08:41.700
I finally feel better now.

01:08:45.704 --> 01:08:48.332
I'm just worried you'll have
a target on your back now.

01:08:48.415 --> 01:08:50.543
Your life at the hospital going forward

01:08:50.626 --> 01:08:51.669
won't be easy.

01:08:51.752 --> 01:08:53.754
It's fine. I'll just quit.

01:08:53.838 --> 01:08:54.755
What?

01:08:55.923 --> 01:08:58.592
Dr. Ku, aren't you angry?
Aren't you pissed?

01:08:58.676 --> 01:09:00.302
Are you some kind of saint?

01:09:00.386 --> 01:09:01.470
I'm a pushover.

01:09:02.012 --> 01:09:03.013
Do-won the Pushover.

01:09:03.889 --> 01:09:04.765
Have you forgotten?

01:09:05.558 --> 01:09:07.017
What are you talking about?

01:09:10.187 --> 01:09:12.314
Damn it.
Just thinking about it makes me mad.

01:09:15.276 --> 01:09:17.528
You f***ing piece of s***.

01:09:18.154 --> 01:09:20.447
Have you lost your damn mind?

01:09:20.531 --> 01:09:23.450
How dare you open your yap
and say that, you son of a b****?

01:09:28.664 --> 01:09:30.708
Did you memorize that?

01:09:30.791 --> 01:09:31.959
It was easy to remember.

01:09:32.042 --> 01:09:34.336
You're good. You have a knack for it.

01:09:34.420 --> 01:09:36.338
As soon as I heard it,
it rolled off the tongue.

01:09:37.089 --> 01:09:38.841
I must have a knack for swearing.

01:09:44.847 --> 01:09:46.515
I thought you liked me.

01:09:47.224 --> 01:09:48.184
I guess not anymore?

01:09:50.728 --> 01:09:53.105
I mean, who talks like that
in front of someone they like?

01:09:56.984 --> 01:09:58.569
I guess you don't like me anymore.

01:09:58.652 --> 01:09:59.653
That's not true.

01:10:01.530 --> 01:10:03.365
I still like you.

01:10:07.161 --> 01:10:10.372
I'm someone who still curses
in front of people I like.

01:10:15.085 --> 01:10:16.045
I guess I'm a lunatic.

01:10:23.677 --> 01:10:25.179
Then can you say that again?

01:10:29.183 --> 01:10:30.184
Really?

01:10:41.862 --> 01:10:44.782
Can I like you?

01:10:58.087 --> 01:10:59.338
No, not that.

01:11:08.097 --> 01:11:10.474
Like, "Piece of crap." That stuff?

01:11:20.567 --> 01:11:23.070
Listen carefully. I'm only saying it once.

01:11:23.153 --> 01:11:23.988
Okay.

01:11:26.448 --> 01:11:28.951
You f***ing piece of s***.

01:11:29.660 --> 01:11:31.787
You've lost your damn mind!

01:11:31.870 --> 01:11:34.999
How dare you open your yap
and say that, you son of a b****?

01:11:41.213 --> 01:11:42.548
That damn bastard.

01:11:44.675 --> 01:11:45.926
What a load of crap.

01:11:46.010 --> 01:11:47.136
She didn't say that.

01:11:47.219 --> 01:11:48.387
I added that one.

01:13:04.129 --> 01:13:08.092
THANKS TO OUR SPECIAL GUEST,
BAE HYEON-SEONG, OUR ETERNAL JANG HONG-DO

01:13:08.175 --> 01:13:11.387
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

01:13:11.470 --> 01:13:13.597
You're already preparing
to recruit interns?

01:13:13.680 --> 01:13:15.849
Our current first-years
didn't turn out well at all.

01:13:15.933 --> 01:13:17.810
They're all a bit unwell.

01:13:18.811 --> 01:13:20.396
Are you laughing? You think it's funny?

01:13:21.647 --> 01:13:24.400
I mean, how many times are you going
to call Anesthesiology today?

01:13:24.483 --> 01:13:26.652
I know, but please, just this once.

01:13:26.735 --> 01:13:27.778
-She's here.
-She's here.

01:13:27.861 --> 01:13:30.030
You said it wasn't coming today.

01:13:30.114 --> 01:13:32.658
If they're duds next year too,
we're all screwed.

01:13:33.534 --> 01:13:35.661
You go on leave tomorrow. Right, Dr. Ku?

01:13:35.744 --> 01:13:37.454
Don't call me and ask, "Where are you?"

01:13:37.538 --> 01:13:38.497
Especially you, Jae-il.

01:13:38.580 --> 01:13:40.416
You're gone for three days,
not three months.

01:13:40.499 --> 01:13:41.542
Don't you worry.

01:13:41.625 --> 01:13:42.626
Bye.

01:13:43.293 --> 01:13:46.088
Anytime we ask something,
they say to ask the chief resident.

01:13:46.171 --> 01:13:48.257
How many times can we say
Ku Do-won's not here?

01:13:49.675 --> 01:13:51.802
-Geez, OB!
-Why is he mad?

01:13:51.885 --> 01:13:54.179
It's to tell you no.

01:13:54.263 --> 01:13:55.931
Then should we not call you?

01:13:56.014 --> 01:13:57.933
They think we're fools,
because we hold back.

01:13:58.016 --> 01:14:00.936
Right, being patient three times
is too much.

01:14:01.019 --> 01:14:02.521
You'll just go mad.

01:14:02.604 --> 01:14:03.439
No!

01:14:05.441 --> 01:14:06.400
Does your stomach hurt?

01:14:06.483 --> 01:14:08.485
They're in emergency surgery.
What do we do?

01:14:19.037 --> 01:14:21.039
Subtitle translation by: Jamie Jin
